[18.56,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[54.399,"o","note: the region eu-south-2 does not offer c6a.xlarge, the template's default for InstanceType: using c5.xlarge (--aws-instance-type picks another)\r\n"]
[55.097,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what ov does in your AWS account (region eu-south-2); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. SSH key: import the stack's own key pair into the region (.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-pro-a102129-key.pem)\r\n  2. Template: render the single node template into .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-singlenode.yaml\r\n     and its parameters into .openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json (0600)\r\n  3. Bucket: stage the template in the S3 bucket openvidu-cfn-templates-***-eu-south-2 (created once, reused by every stack)\r\n  4. Network: the region's default VPC, vpc-0e2358cb016b9fef5 (the template places the machine there)\r\n  5. Machines: Create the CloudFormation stack openvidu-e2e-aws-pro-a102129 with the machine, which installs OpenVidu Pro on itself (about 5 minutes)\r\n  6. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n\r\n▶ Create the machines on AWS…\r\n   · SSH key pair for this stack: .openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-pro-a102129-key.pem\r\n"]
[55.871,"o","   · import its public half into eu-south-2 as the key pair openvidu-e2e-aws-pro-a102129-key\r\n"]
[58.251,"o","   · create the CloudFormation stack openvidu-e2e-aws-pro-a102129 from .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-singlenode.yaml (this returns when CloudFormation is done)\r\n"]
[474.008,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so `ov stack destroy` removes it even if the wait below fails\r\n   ✓ Create the machines on AWS\r\n\r\n▶ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu…\r\n"]
